  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Dry and unseasonably warm weather\nconditions take hold over Nevada as the low pressure that gave\nrain pushes east across the four corners, while a high pressure\ncreeps in right behind it and will strengthen across the southwest\nby mid-week. Temperatures will gradually warm to being several\ndegrees above normal with unseasonably warm temperatures by Friday\nand over the weekend, reaching close to 15 degrees above normal\nfor this time of year. Winds will be light around 5-10 mph with\ngusts up to 20 mph each afternoon.\n\nBy the start of next week, models show slight cooling as a weak\nupper level trough moves over the western CONUS that will help\nweaken the high pressure system, however conditions expected to\nremain dry and still be above normal temperatures.",
